; expect 63
; The five atomic primitives, single-threaded and without the standard
; library: `__atomic_store`, `__atomic_add`, `__atomic_cas`,
; `__atomic_load` and `__fence`, on a word of an `__alloc`ed block.
;
; The answer is a bitmask, one bit per fact, so a compiler that gets
; one of them wrong names the fact rather than answering a number near
; the right one:
;
;    1  `__atomic_add` answers the word BEFORE the add
;    2  a compare-and-swap whose expectation holds answers that word
;    4  one whose expectation fails answers the word it found, and
;       stored nothing - the word is still 50 below, not 99
;    8  `__atomic_load` sees the atomic writes
;   16  a plain `__load64` sees them too: the atomic and the plain view
;       of one word agree
;   32  `__atomic_load` takes a BYTE address where `__load64` takes a
;       base and a word index - word 1 of the block is at `p + 8`
;
; `__fence` stands between the writes and the reads, and its answer -
; 0 - is ADDED INTO THE SUM rather than dropped, deliberately. It is
; spelled bare here, as the formatter's normal form spells every
; nullary primitive (`__argc`, `__axiom_arena_mark`), and `(__fence)`
; reaches the emitter as the same bare variable reference: a nullary
; primitive the emitter does not recognise there emits `%__fence`,
; which is nothing at all in statement position and an llc error the
; moment the value is used. It was nothing at all in this file's first
; draft, and the fixture passed with no fence emitted.
; `tests/stdlib/440-atomics.ax` prints the same answer.
(:: bit (-> Bool Int Int))

(fn (bit ok n)
  (if ok
    n
    0
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((p (__alloc 16)))
    {
      (__atomic_store p 40)
      (__store64 p 1 7)
      (let (
        (fenced __fence)
        (old (__atomic_add p 2))
        (hit (__atomic_cas p 42 50))
        (miss (__atomic_cas p 42 99))
        (now (__atomic_load p))
        (plain (__load64 p 0))
        (word1 (__atomic_load (+ p 8)))
        (b1 (bit (== old 40) 1))
        (b2 (bit (== hit 42) 2))
        (b4 (bit (== miss 50) 4))
        (b8 (bit (== now 50) 8))
        (b16 (bit (== plain 50) 16))
        (b32 (bit (== word1 7) 32))
      )
        (+ fenced (+ b1 (+ b2 (+ b4 (+ b8 (+ b16 b32))))))
      )
    }
  )
)
